    ],
    [
      200.25,
      319.5,
      1275.270263671875,
      345.0255126953125,
      "There was also an additional initiative that had not been originally planned, but which became\n",
      1,
      0
    ],
    [
      200.25,
      351.0,
      1379.025146484375,
      536.2755126953125,
      "a central feature of the programme. This was when farmers started to dig holes for tanks in\nthe fenced-off areas and to fill these with water and use them for breeding fish — an important\nQ38\nsource of protein. After a time, another suggestion was made by local people which hadn't\nbeen part of the programme’s original proposal, but which was also adopted later on. They\ndecided to try setting up colonies of bees, which would provide honey both for their own\nQ39\nconsumption and to sell.\n",
      2,
      0
    ],
    [
      201.75,
      558.0,
      1274.490234375,
      647.2769775390625,
      "So what lessons can be learned from this programme? First of all, it tells us that in dry,\narid regions, if there is access to a reliable source of water, there is great potential for the\ndevelopment of agriculture. In Chicualacuala, there was a marked improvement in agricultural\n",
      3,
      0
    ],
    [
      202.5,
      651.75,
      1379.8798828125,
      768.770263671875,
      "production, which improved food security and benefited local people by providing them with\nboth food and income. However, it's important to set realistic timelines for each phase of the\nprogramme, especially for its design, as mistakes made at this stage may be hard to correct\nQ40\nlater on.\n",
      4,
      0
    ],
    [
      201.0,
      795.0,
      1234.215087890625,
      822.0269775390625,
      "The programme demonstrates that sustainable development is possible in areas where ...\n",
      5,
      0
